n class=\"fn\">m</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.LawfulDeterministicIterator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":1003,"name":"Std.LawfulDeterministicIterator.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.lean#L1003-L1019"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">class</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.LawfulDeterministicIterator\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">LawfulDeterministicIterator</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">m</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w → <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> w'</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Iterator\">Iterator</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span>]</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Prop</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"This typeclass characterizes iterators that have deterministic return values. This typeclass does\n*not* guarantee that there are no monadic side effects such as exceptions.\n\nGeneral monadic iterators can be nondeterministic, so that `it.IsPlausibleStep step` will be true\nfor no or more than one choice of `step`. This typeclass ensures that there is exactly one such\nchoice.\n\nThis