Iterators/Basic.html#Std.IterM.IsPlausibleSkipSuccessorOf\">Std.IterM.IsPlausibleSkipSuccessorOf</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Iterators.Productive\">Std.Iterators.Productive</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">m</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Iterators.Productive.mk","kind":"ctor","line":876,"name":"Std.Iterators.Productive.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.lean#L876-L885"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">class</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Iterators.Productive\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Iterators</span>.<span class=\"name\">Productive</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">m</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1 → <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_2</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Iterator\">Iterator</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span>]</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Prop</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`Productive α m` asserts that `IterM (α := α) m` terminates or emits a value after finitely many\nskips. Technically, this m