class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Shrink.deflate\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Shrink</span>.<span class=\"name\">deflate</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Shrink\">Shrink</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Converts elements of `α` into elements of `Shrink α`. ","docLink":"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Shrink.deflate","kind":"def","line":47,"name":"Std.Shrink.deflate","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.lean#L47-L50"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Shrink\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Shrink</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u</div></div>","info":{"doc":"Currently, `Shrink α` is just a wrapper around `α`.\n\nIn the future, `Shrink` should allow shrinking `α` into a potentially smaller universe,\ngiven a proof that `α` is actually small, just like Mathlib's `Shrink`, except that\nthe latter's conversion functions are noncomputable. Until then, `Shrink α` is always in the\nsame universe as `α`.\n\nThis no-op type exists so that fewer breaking changes will be needed when the\nreal `Shrink` type is available and the iterators will be made more flexible with regard to\nuniverses.\n\nThe conversion functions `Shrink.deflate` and\n`Shrink.inflate` form an equivalence between\n`α` and `Shrink α`, but this equivalence is intentionally not definitional.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Shrink","kind":"def","line":29,"name":"Std.Shrink","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.lean#L29-L45"}}],"imports":["Init.Ext","Init.NotationExtra","Init.PropLemmas","Init.WFTactics"],"instances":[{"className":"WellFoundedRelation","name":"Std.IterM.TerminationMeasures.instWellFoundedRelationFinite","typeNames":["Std.IterM.TerminationMeasures.Finite"]},{"className":"WellFoundedRelation","name":"Std.IterM.TerminationMeasures.instWellFoundedRelationProductive","typeNames":["Std.IterM.TerminationMeasures.Productive"]},{"className":"Std.Iterators.Productive","name":"Std.Iterators.instProductiveOfFinte","typeNames":[]}],"name":"Init.Data.Iterators.Basic"}